<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of four-day English county</p>
<p>championship cricket matches on Friday:</p>
<p>At Edgbaston: Essex beat Warwickshire by 170 runs. Essex 238</p>
<p>and 450-6 declared. Warwickshire 253 and 265. Essex 21 points</p>
<p>Warwickshire 6.</p>
<p>At Trent Bridge: Leicestershire beat Nottinghamshire by six</p>
<p>wickets. Nottinghamshire 324 and 196.  Leicestershire 439 and</p>
<p>82-4. Leicestershire 24 points Nottinghamshire 6.</p>
<p>At The Oval: Surrey beat Northamptonshire by 225 runs.</p>
<p>Surrey 395 and 298. Northamptonshire 235 and 233. Surrey 24</p>
<p>points Northamptonshire 5.</p>
<p>At Southampton: Hampshire v Glamorgan match drawn. Glamorgan</p>
<p>401 and 281-6 declared (O.Gibson 62 not out), Hampshire 352-4</p>
<p>declared and 261-8 (R.Smith 91, W.Kendall 71). Hampshire 11</p>
<p>points Glamorgan 8.</p>
<p>At Taunton: Somerset v Derbyshire match drawn. Derbyshire</p>
<p>524 and 322-6 declared (K.Barnett 141, D.Jones 74). Somerset 464</p>
<p>and 296-8 (J.Kerr 68 not out, P.Bowler 60, M.Lathwell 54; D.Cork</p>
<p>4-55). Somerset and Derbyshire 10 points.</p>
</text>
